{%- comment -%}
  App Embed Block (target: body) — real-user Core Web Vitals monitoring
  ("Web Vitals (RUM)"), plus the AI-referral beacon.

  This embed carries BOTH measurements the app takes on a live pageview. The
  referral beacon started out in structured-data.liquid and moved here: JSON-LD
  is markup a merchant may legitimately switch off, and switching off markup
  must not silently switch off the visit counter. Both beacons live in
  assets/web-vitals.js (assets are served statically and do not count towards
  the extension's 100 KiB Liquid budget).

  Loads a small client-side script that observes LCP, CLS, INP, FCP and TTFB
  for the current pageview via the browser's PerformanceObserver APIs, then
  sends ONE beacon per pageview (on visibilitychange→hidden / pagehide) to the
  app proxy at /apps/contentpilot/web-vitals. The server aggregates samples
  per (template, device) and surfaces them in ContentPilot → SEO → Ladezeit
  ("Echte Besucherdaten") alongside the on-demand PageSpeed Insights audit.

  Privacy: NO visitor identifiers and NO cookies are set or read. Each sample
  carries only the page path, the theme template name, a coarse device class
  (mobile/desktop derived from viewport width), the observed metric values,
  and a short CSS-selector-like label for the element responsible for
  LCP/CLS/INP (e.g. "img#hero.banner") — never any personal data.

  Template name: `template.name` is the documented Liquid global for the
  active theme template ("product", "collection", "index", "page", "article",
  "blog", "search", "404", ...) and is available wherever `request` is (this
  extension's other body-target blocks — see structured-data.liquid,
  social-meta.liquid — already read `request.page_type` from the same
  rendering context). `request.page_type` is used as a fallback in case a
  theme ever renders this app block somewhere `template` is unset.

  The embed being active is the on/off switch — no other settings needed.
{%- endcomment -%}

<script>
  window.__cpWebVitals = {
    endpoint: '/apps/contentpilot/web-vitals',
    referralEndpoint: '/apps/contentpilot/ai-referral',
    template: {{ template.name | default: request.page_type | json }}
  };
</script>
<script src="{{ 'web-vitals.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Web Vitals (RUM)",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Collects real visitor Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, INP) for ContentPilot's SEO speed report, and counts visits that arrive from an AI assistant (ChatGPT, Perplexity, ...) for the AI search report. No visitor identifiers or cookies are used. Enable once - no placement or configuration needed."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
